{"id": 8356980, "full_name": "Brian T. Emmer", "first_name": "Brian T.", "last_name": "Emmer", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://plos.figshare.com/articles/figure/Quality_analysis_of_genome-wide_ACE2_CRISPR_screens_/19287233", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<p>(A-B) Cumulative distribution functions of normalized read counts for each gRNA in ACE2-sorted populations in 4 independent biologic replicates of the genome-wide primary CRISPR screen of wild-type (A) and ACE2-enriched (B) HuH7 cells. (C) Mean log<sub>2</sub> fold-change of each individual gRNA targeting ACE2, the aggregate mean of these individual ACE2-targeting gRNAs, and a violin plot of the distribution for all 1000 control nontargeting gRNAS (lines indicate quartiles) in the genome-wide ACE2 CRISPR screens of wild-type (C) and ACE2-enriched (D) HuH7 cells. (E-H) Q-Q plots of observed versus expected\u2013log(p) for positive (E,G) or negative (F, H) regulation of ACE2 surface abundance for every gene in the primary genome-wide CRISPR screen of HuH7 wild-type (E-F) or ACE2-enriched (G-H) cells. Observed p-values were calculated by MAGeCK gene-level analysis.</p> <p>(TIF)</p>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 801846, "created_date": "2022-03-01T18:39:32Z", "modified_date": "2023-06-12T05:53:22Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["viral spike protein", "throughput crispr screens", "suggest potential targets", "influence cellular susceptibility", "immortalized cell lines", "established transcription factors", "cell type specificity", "3 cells revealed", "host factors involved", "derived huh7 cells", "div >< p", "ace2 regulatory networks", "ace2 modifiers comprised", "ace2 surface abundan